ily without a trade deal  with the eu  so given that confidence will the  government publish its full economic  impact assessment  on the implications if no trade deal is  achieved broken down by industry and  broken down  by the regions and nations of our united  kingdom  it may at least help us to understand  what we're supposed to be planning for  and while the government lectures  businesses about being match fit  the government's own preparations are  badly off-pace  so let's look at those in late july the  government announced 50 million pounds  of funding for customs intermediaries  could the minister update the house with  how much of this the funds  businesses have drawn down and the  latest figures for the number of customs  agents  trained up to be ready for the 1st of  january  the government have given authorisation  for a number of lorry parks so how many  of these  inland border facilities as the minister  likes to call them has been started work  on  and how many are now completed of the  i.t systems needed  can the minister list how many have been  um how many  um are on track and whether the crucial  goods vehicle movement system  has been tested with all haulage  businesses  the minister mentions business  preparedness so let me just touch  on that what is happening in terms of  security  and what is happening in terms of data  sharing i'll just conclude  mr speaker this government must deliver  a deal which provides guarantees and  safeguards on workers rights  environmental standards  and animal welfare protect jobs and do  nothing to jeopardize the good friday  agreement this was all promised last  year  time is short so my message to  government is blunt stop posturing  start negotiating and prop deliver the  deal that you promised to the british  people  [Applause]  i'm very grateful to the honourable lady  for her questions and she  she made the point that uh uh with  respect to an oven ready deal that the  withdrawal agreement  of course wa